   |A| are principal values of 3 g_N^2 Tr_block(T_i T_j)/[J(J+1)(2J+1)], the A.A^T reduction at the isotope named -- magnitudes only, since it is quadratic. A.g is Tr_block(mu.T) normalized: +-1 means T is proportional to mu on the block (exact inside a free-ion J manifold) and its sign is the relative sign of A and g. The stored operator is T itself, in Eh/mu_N, so the isotope may be changed by the consumer 
 *** WARNING [props.dump] the property operators L and S carry NO picture-change transformation : they are the bare non-relativistic AO operators used unchanged in the two-component basis. This matches OpenMolcas RASSI, so a cross-code comparison is like-for-like. The approximation has been measured and is small: below 0.3% on every free-ion multiplet g factor from Z=5 to Z=81, 0.02% on a 3d complex's ground doublet, and it splits no degeneracy at all. It is recorded in the header of ticl3.props
 *** WARNING [props.dump] ticl3.props carries HYPERFINE FIELD operators for Ti1. They are the isotope-independent operator T in Eh/mu_N, always X2C picture-changed, with the unperturbed transformation and no two-electron picture change; H_hf = sum_k g_N(k) sum_u T_k_u (x) I_k_u, and the nuclear-spin algebra and any A tensor belong to the consumer. The isotropic part comes from core-s spin polarization, which a VALENCE active space does not carry, so judge it against the active space in the header

