   these |A| are NOT a prediction: a valence 3d active space carries no core-s
   spin polarization, so the isotropic part of a transition-metal hyperfine
   coupling is qualitatively wrong. What the agreement tests is the machinery.
   Kuiva never builds the electron-nuclear product space named above -- it
   writes the electronic matrices and the nuclear table, and the consumer
   chooses the isotope. The dimension is reported for that reason only.

